b-hamburg-38/\">The Beatles live: Indra Club, Hamburg</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=9b5604cb06f54325d9a73116957d9337&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=6612&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "Studio Two, EMI Studios, Abbey Road\nProducer: Chris Thomas\nEngineer: Ken ScottOne of the White Album’s highlights, ‘Happiness Is A Warm Gun’, had its first recording session on this evening. \n\n\n\nThe session took place from 7pm-3am. The Beatles recorded 45 takes of the song, which had the working title ‘Happiness Is A Warm Gun In Your Hand’. John Lennon played electric guitar and sang a guide vocal, George Harrison was on another electric guitar, Paul McCartney played bass, and Ringo Starr was on drums.The song’s various changes in tempo and time signature resulting in a number of breakdowns. The following evening they taped another 25 attempts, which eventually resulted in a usable backing track.Lyrics for Happiness Is A Warm Gun, transcribed by Mal Evans\nPage last updated: 23 June 2023Also on this day...2025: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Yaamava’ Theater, Highland2023: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Fox Theatre, St Louis2022: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Hartford HealthCare Amphitheater, Bridgeport2018: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Ordway Center for the Performing Arts, Saint Paul2017: Paul McCartney live: Carrier Dome, Syracuse2013: Paul McCartney live: El Capitan Outdoor Stage, Los Angeles (Jimmy Kimmel Live)2005: Paul McCartney live: Wachovia Center, Philadelphia2003: Paul McCartney live: Adopt-A-Minefield Gala, Los Angeles2002: Paul McCartney live: Xcel Energy Center, Saint Paul1993: Paul McCartney live: Hanns-Martin-Schleyer-Halle, Stuttgart1980: Recording: Hard Times Are Over, Every Man Has A Woman Who Loves Him, Give Me Something by John Lennon and Yoko Ono1980: Recording: Dead Giveaway by Ringo Starr1975: Wings live: Caird Hall, Dundee1974: Mixing: Walls And Bridges by John Lennon1974: Travel: John Lennon – San Francisco to New York City1974: US single release: Whatever Gets You Thru The Night by John Lennon1970: Travel: Paul McCartney – Nice to Monaco1967: Filming: Magical Mystery Tour1